MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_001: Sprinkling the solution with glirmosa helps prevent\npests? I didn't know that!
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_002: So that's how you grew such gorgeous vegetables!\nI'll buy a whole bag, please!
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_003: Hi, Halvin. Doing some shopping?
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_004: Oh, hi! Yeah, I was just buying veggies from a lady\nwho grew them herself.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_005: Just look at these shem yams! They're so big and\nround and shiny.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_006: Seems like she did a great job growing them. I asked\nher for tips on pest control too.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_007: Heh. You really are a farmer's daughter, hm?\nYou take interest in things most people overlook.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_008: Ahaha... Yeah, it's kind of embarrassing... But I\ndo love gardening and stuff...
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_009: I feel like I might even figure out how to make my\nparents' work easier.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_010: It can be very hard to create food... I'm sure you and\nyour family struggled plenty.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_011: Well, it's not all hardship. I actually enjoy tilling,\nand I love seeing the veggies grow.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_012: If that whole mess with the landowner hadn't\nhappened, I probably wouldn't have left my parents.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_013: He treated you poorly, didn't he? And you were\nasked to marry someone you didn't have feelings for.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_014: Yeah... I really couldn't take it. So...I left.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_015: Sometimes I do wonder if I should've just gone with\nit or something.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_016: No, you did the right thing. You shouldn't marry\nsomeone you don't care for.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_017: I can empathize with you. I ran away too.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_018: You did?
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_019: Yes. If I was following our village's customs, I would\nhave been married by now.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_020: But among the options in my village, there was\nnobody I liked in that way.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_021: Plus, I wanted to watch over Anatolia. So I joined\nher and set out to serve as a Protector to her.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_022: I never knew all that... Seems like we might be kinda\nsimilar, me and you.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_023: Mhm. We're both very nurturing and good with\nkids too.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_024: You have four younger brothers and sisters, right? I\nused to babysit in the village too.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_025: Oh, really? That's interesting. Maybe our paths were\nmeant to cross.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_026: This has been lovely. I hope we get more chances to\nspend time together.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_C_027: The feeling's mutual! I look forward to getting to\nknow you more, Sha Lan.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_001: When selling your veggies, it's smart to let the\ncustomer sample them, so they know what to expect.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_002: Color and visual appearance can fetch a higher price,\neven if the taste isn't the best... Mhm.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_003: You're so studious! Are you making notes from what\nthe merchant taught you?
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_004: Sure am. I'll need this info in the future, so I'm\nkeeping a record of what I've learned.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_005: It sounded like it was more focused on the business\nside of things rather than growing the vegetables.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_006: Do you have an interest in selling vegetables too?
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_007: I mean...that sounds nice enough, but I actually have\na different dream.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_008: It might seem kinda silly, but I hope to buy my own\nplot of land eventually.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_009: I'd bring my parents and siblings to the farm, and\nwe'd grow yummy veggies and make a living.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_010: Aw, that's such a nice dream you have! I'm sure\nyour family will love that.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_011: And with your own land, you wouldn't have to deal\nwith tyrannical landowners...
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_012: Yeah! Right now I'm just a humble sharecropper.\nI know my dream is kinda far-fetched...
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_013: It isn't far-fetched at all! You're working so hard.\nI know you'll make it happen!
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_014: You think so? Maybe if you believe in it, then it\nreally can happen...
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_015: I feel happy, hearing that. You're always so\nencouraging... I really look up to you.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_016: Oh, you're so sweet... Truthfully, I feel a bit envious\nof you.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_017: I've never had such big dreams...
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_018: Maybe that's because you're grounded and realistic.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_019: It's not even that. I'm not really capable of thinking\nabout the future.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_020: I became a Protector because I didn't want Anatolia\ngetting hurt.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_021: And I left the village because I didn't want to stay\nonly to marry someone I didn't love.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_022: I'm always reacting to the present moment. That's\nwhere you and I are different.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_023: I see...
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_024: Um, I don't really know much about your\nhometown, but...
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_025: I don't think being so present minded is a bad thing.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_026: You think you don't have a dream, but maybe it's\njust that you haven't found it yet.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_027: I guess that could be...
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_028: Yeah. You'll find your way. I know you'll figure it out.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_029: Aw, thank you, Halvin. Now you're the one\nencouraging me.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_B_030: You'd do the same. In fact, you did! Thank you,\nSha Lan!
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_001: Thank you for sharing with me. I'll use this as a\nframe of reference.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_002: Who were you talking to just now? I've never met\nhim before.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_003: He runs a restaurant nearby. He was telling me about\nhis experiences as a restaurant owner.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_004: Oh! Have you found your dream, then?
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_005: Heh. You noticed, huh? I guess I was copying what\nyou did before—gathering information.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_006: Copying me?! Aw, I'm embarrassed... But that also\nmakes me feel kinda good!
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_007: So tell me about your dream for the future.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_008: I want to run my own restaurant.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_009: Everyone could come eat delicious food. And I won't\naccept payment from children who can't afford it.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_010: I've taken care of kids who didn't have much. I've\nseen starvation... I want to help somehow.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_011: I know the idea is a bit out there... The business\nprobably won't survive if I'm not charging everyone...
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_012: It isn't out there! You're working so hard. I know\nyou'll make it happen!
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_013: Hehe. I remember saying something similar to\nyou once.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_014: My dream will come true, and so will yours, Sha Lan!
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_015: I hope so. The war is ongoing, but I can't give\nup hope.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_016: Before, I'd only think about the present moment,\nnever focusing on my own dreams.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_017: But thanks to you, I'm able to look ahead to\nthe future. You inspired me.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_018: Seriously?! But I'm always inspired by you!
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_019: I've got an idea! If our dreams come true...
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_020: You can use the veggies I grow in your dishes!\nI'll bring you the best of the best!
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_021: That sounds fantastic! Maybe I should build my\nrestaurant right next to your farm.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_022: Meals made with freshly picked vegetables—it'll be\ndelicious!
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_023: Yeah! That would be amazing! I hope tons of people\ncome to your restaurant.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_024: Hey, Sha Lan... You and me, we've both been\nthrough a lot.
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_025: I'm happy we're still here, still breathing. We're\ngoing to have an amazing future together!
MID_SE_Sar_Hal_A_026: Yes, we will. Me and you.